From: Sukrit Jaidee <45908411+SukritJaAIproject@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 09:08:31 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] feat(fault-detection): add AI Fault Intelligence
 dashboard

New /dashboard/ai/fault-detection page: research overview with published /
strict / ISO-reviewed label snapshots, five-detector leaderboard, SLAC timing,
label lineage, fleet and per-station fault donuts (45 stations), station
detail dialog, fault glossary, and the .pcap/.pcapng upload workflow. The old
"Ai Module" sub-navigation is replaced and the sidebar entry now points at the
new page. Font stack moves to Kanit (Thai) / Plus Jakarta Sans / JetBrains Mono;
the remote font-awesome/Prompt imports and the nepcha analytics script are
dropped from the root layout.

Implemented with Codex 2026-09-17..22 and committed from the working tree as
handed over. Frontend tests: 150/150 passing.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
